; [CHOSEN, not recovered] - input to `lib /def:` so this image can statically IMPORT from the shipped
; binkw32.dll (RAD Game Tools' Bink SDK) rather than resolve it at run time. The shipped RendDX9.dll
; carries a static import descriptor for binkw32 with these ten entries, so a static import keeps the
; replacement's dependency list identical to the original (visible to `dumpbin /dependents`).
;
; The names are the __stdcall-decorated export names copied VERBATIM from `dumpbin /imports RendDX9.dll`
; (leading underscore + @<byteCount>). A C++ `extern "C" __stdcall` declaration of each Bink function
; (see Bink.h) mangles to exactly these strings, which is what lets a plain declaration bind against
; the 2000s-era DLL - the same trick Memory.def uses for the mangled bf_malloc names.
;
; Only the ten functions the shipped image actually imports are listed. binkw32.dll ships in the game
; directory alongside BF2.exe.
LIBRARY binkw32
EXPORTS
    _BinkOpen@8
    _BinkClose@4
    _BinkDoFrame@4
    _BinkCopyToBuffer@28
    _BinkNextFrame@4
    _BinkWait@4
    _BinkGetSummary@8
    _BinkPause@8
    _BinkSetSoundSystem@8
    _BinkOpenDirectSound@4
